## Diagnosis

The failure is a **compile error, not an assertion failure**:

```
# fixture/buildcodecompile/tests/suite_test [fixture/buildcodecompile/tests/suite.test]
tests/suite/multiply_test.go:13:14: undefined: calc.Multiply
FAIL	fixture/buildcodecompile/tests/suite [build failed]
```

`tests/suite/multiply_test.go` imports `fixture/buildcodecompile/services/calc` and calls `calc.Multiply(2, 3)`. The production package `services/calc` (package `calc`, file `services/calc/calc.go`) declares only `Add`. The identifier `Multiply` is not declared anywhere in the package, so the external test package `suite_test` fails to build.

Because Go reports a non-compiling test package as a **single package-level build failure**, every test in `tests/suite` is blocked, not just the multiply one. There is exactly one missing symbol, so there is exactly one repair.

Per `docs/architecture/architecture.yaml`, the `calc` service's `path: services/calc` is the only write root. Per `CLAUDE.md`, `tests/suite/` is the specification and must not be touched.

